= Heat <ch_heat>
== Newton

The short paper which follows was published anonymously in the _Philosophical Transactions, Abridged_, Vol. II. Its author was known to be Newton (p. 30) and it is given as his in his _Opuscula_. It is dated 1701. Newton's thermometer was graduated by the use of two fixed points and may have been the first one of the sort with which useful observations were made, though others had suggested the same method of graduation, particularly DalencÃ© in 1688 in his _Traittez des baromÃ¨tres, thermomÃ¨tres et notiomÃ¨tres_. The paper contains also Newton's law of cooling.

=== A Scale of the Degrees of Heat

